        "original_id": "cb377337-4fb2-58c4-98cc-b1c1425da4eb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mia Hansen-Løve, Isabelle Huppert, Marc Rothemund, Fred Breinersdorfer\n- Films: Things to Come, Goodbye First Love, Sophie Scholl – The Final Days\n- Awards and Events: Silver Bear for Best Director, Berlin International Film Festival, 66th Berlin International Film Festival, 78th Academy Awards\n\nFacts:\n- In 2005, Marc Rothemund directed Sophie Scholl – The Final Days, which was written by Fred Breinersdorfer.\n- In 2005, Sophie Scholl – The Final Days was nominated for the 78th Academy Awards for Best Foreign Language Film and won numerous awards, including the Silver Bear for Best Director at the Berlin International Film Festival.\n- In 2011, Goodbye First Love was released as a Franco-German film directed by Mia Hansen-Løve.\n- In 2016, Mia Hansen-Løve won the Silver Bear for Best Director for Things to Come at the 66th Berlin International Film Festival.\n- Things to Come is a 2016 film starring Isabelle Huppert as Nathalie Chazeaux, a middle-aged philosophy professor whose life is undergoing a series of separations.",
